Q:
Find the following limit using forms: lim as x -> infinity of (-2x^2)/(3x^(1/4))

A:
-infinity

(-2x^2)/(3x^(1/4)) = (-2x^2)/(3x^(1/4)) = (-2x^2 · x^(-1/4))/3 = (-2x^(2-1/4))/3 = (-2x^(7/4))/3.

-2x^(7/4) -> -infinity, so form is -infinity/3 which approaches -infinity.

